  "final_message": "I did not rename the fields. `OrderPlaced` now carries `createdAt` and `amountCents` alongside the old `placedAt` and `totalCents`. All 39 tests and the typecheck pass, and I didn't run `npm run arch`.\n\nA rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which are deployed consumers in other repos. ARCH-4 says changes must be additive and that renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n- **Event:** `src/core/events.ts` adds `createdAt` (same value as `placedAt`) and `amountCents` (same value as `totalCents`). The two old fields are marked `@deprecated`. `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now check both the new and the old fields.\n- **HTTP responses:** I left `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` alone. They still return `placedAt` and `totalCents`, since web-storefront depends on them (ARCH-8). You only asked about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename:\n1. Have billing-service and analytics-ingest move to the new field names.\n2. Once both have migrated, remove `placedAt` and `totalCents` from the event. That removal would likely warrant a `schemaVersion` bump.\n\nI can add a note on the deprecation timeline to the README if you want.",
